{
  "_comment": [
    "The response contract for a money turn on POST /api/v1/chat.",
    "",
    "Every key listed in `keys` is always present, including `receipt`, which is",
    "null when nothing moved. `forbidden_keys` are never present: the old",
    "approval-card protocol (requires_confirmation + cards) is gone, and a client",
    "that still reads it is reading a contract this server no longer has.",
    "",
    "`examples` are verbatim responses recorded from the endpoint. Pin the Go",
    "PythonChatResponse struct and these examples against this file.",
    "",
    "Request direction: the client settles a challenge with",
    "{ \"confirm_id\": \"<id from this response>\", \"yes\": true|false }.",
    "There is no other way to confirm, and `approved_actions` is not read."
  ],
  "endpoint": "POST /api/v1/chat",
  "keys": [
    "response",
    "conversation_id",
    "trace_id",
    "confirm_id",
    "decision",
    "receipt",
    "conversation_history"
  ],
  "forbidden_keys": [
    "requires_confirmation",
    "cards"
  ],
  "request_keys_for_a_confirmation": [
    "confirm_id",
    "yes"
  ],
